WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:05.605 line:8%
- How typical is it
for voters in this area

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:08.941 line:8%
to see a Republican
candidate blockwalking?

00:00:09.042 --> 00:00:10.877 line:8%
MAYRA FLORES: Yeah, this
is new for them, it is.

00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.679 line:8%
It's probably the first
time in a long time

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.747 line:8%
that they have a Republican
knocking their doors.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:18.517
Prior to 2020, maybe people
weren't as confident in saying

00:00:18.618 --> 00:00:19.618
that they were Republican.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:22.154
But now, people
are confident and

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:23.957
they're not hiding it anymore.

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.892
- For decades, Republicans
wrote off the Rio Grande Valley

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.794
as a Democratic
stronghold, where

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:32.031
overwhelmingly Latino counties
stretch along the Texas border

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:33.266
with Mexico.

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.935
But that changed in 2020
when former President Donald

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:38.604
Trump made serious
gains here and stunned

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:39.939
the political world.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:43.209 line:8%
Now, Republicans are investing
in South Texas candidates,

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.244 line:8%
including many of
Hispanic descent

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:47.880 line:14%
from Congress to County judge.

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:50.216
MAYRA FLORES: This is what
the Republican looks like.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:54.487
It isn't just about, you know,
for the rich or just white

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.421
people.

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.022
- Die hard fan right here.

00:00:57.123 --> 00:00:58.157
MAYRA FLORES: You
follow his page?

00:00:58.258 --> 00:01:00.360
Oh my God, can I give a hug?

00:01:00.460 --> 00:01:01.627
- Yes.

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.628
MAYRA FLORES: How old are you?

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:04.063
- 16, in March I'll be 17.

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.131
MAYRA FLORES: Wow, really.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.566
- Yes, just one more
year and I can vote.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:10.203
MAYRA FLORES: This
area has been voting

00:01:10.303 --> 00:01:13.272
Democrat for over 100 years.

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:15.341
I feel we've been
taken for granted,

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:19.078
we've been loyal to a party
that has done absolutely nothing

00:01:19.179 --> 00:01:20.279
for us.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:23.182
We have families in Mexico
that we are not visiting

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.451
anymore because we're afraid.

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:28.621
So we don't want what
we're afraid to come here.

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:31.390 line:8%
- Republican frontrunner and
first time candidate Mayra

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:33.793 line:8%
Flores is running in
a four-way primary

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.828 line:8%
in one of three
top congressional

00:01:35.929 --> 00:01:37.496 line:14%
races in South Texas.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:41.367
Both the 15th and the 34th
districts are newly redrawn.

00:01:41.468 --> 00:01:43.836 line:8%
And sitting Congressman
Vincente Gonzalez

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.539 line:8%
has switched from the 15th,
which became more favorable

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.475 line:8%
to Republicans, to
run in the 34th,

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.611 line:8%
now more favorable
to Democrats where

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:53.212 line:14%
he will likely face Flores.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.380 line:8%
VINCENTE GONZALEZ:
All the benefits

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:56.583 line:8%
I've had in my
lifetime were created

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.783 line:14%
by the Democratic party.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.520 line:8%
And I think most people in
my region feel the same.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:02.455 line:8%
- Monica De La Cruz
is a second time

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.490 line:8%
Republican candidate,
running for the now

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.859 line:14%
open seat in the 15th district.

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:10.129
In 2020, she came close
to ousting Gonzalez,

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:12.198
the Democratic incumbent here.

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:13.533
MONICA DE LA CRUZ:
Socialists are

00:02:13.633 --> 00:02:18.204
ruining our border security,
our values, and our economy.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:20.173
- De La Cruz was
endorsed by Trump

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:23.376
and has echoed some of his
false claims about voter fraud.

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:26.078
But her central
focus is immigration.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.413 line:8%
MONICA DE LA CRUZ:
President Trump

00:02:27.514 --> 00:02:30.450 line:8%
cared about the border, cared
about border patrol agents

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.351 line:14%
and law enforcement agents.

00:02:32.452 --> 00:02:35.755 line:8%
So in the 2020 election,
people got motivated,

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:39.959 line:8%
were engaged, and
worked to win this seat.

00:02:40.059 --> 00:02:42.494 line:8%
And we came within three
points of doing so.

00:02:42.595 --> 00:02:45.364 line:8%
When I ran, people
said, you're crazy,

00:02:45.465 --> 00:02:49.869 line:8%
this is a Democrat stronghold,
you don't have a chance.

00:02:49.969 --> 00:02:51.804
- Democrats in South
Texas say the claims

00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:54.707
that their party has forgotten
Latino voters are fiction,

00:02:54.807 --> 00:02:56.375
and that Latino
voters were still

00:02:56.476 --> 00:02:59.512
a key part of Biden's
support in major Metropolitan

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:01.914
areas of Texas in 2020.

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:04.684 line:8%
They argue that the party
lost some Latino support

00:03:04.784 --> 00:03:06.786 line:8%
in the border counties
because it largely

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:10.389 line:8%
suspended in-person
campaigning during the pandemic

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:13.126 line:8%
and must do a better job
of connecting with voters

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:15.295 line:8%
on issues like the
border and the future

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:18.998 line:8%
of the oil and gas industry,
which fuels many jobs here.

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.300
MICHELLE VALLEJO: Unfortunately,
the previous administration

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:25.637
showed up to use our
border wall as a photo op.

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.973
And it worked because
it ended up on the TV.

00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:30.910 line:8%
Approaching the border and
immigration conversation

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.947 line:8%
in that way is
divisive, and it takes

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:35.547 line:8%
away from the
actual conversation

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.949 line:14%
we should be having.

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:39.552
- Democrats who have long had
a diverse slate of candidates

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:43.289
in South Texas are confident
they can reverse GOP momentum

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:47.894
here in 2002 now that they are
back campaigning intensively

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.361
in these communities.

00:03:49.462 --> 00:03:52.098
Both sides have long
acknowledged that the Latino

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.632
vote is not a monolith.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:57.269
The November election will test
whether the GOP can maintain

00:03:57.370 --> 00:04:01.140
the gains they made among
Latino voters in key states,

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:03.175
when Trump is not on the ballot.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:04.510
MAYRA FLORES: We
are the forgotten,

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:07.846
and Bronzeville has
been the forgotten.

00:04:07.947 --> 00:04:11.650
I am not here to represent
a political party,

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.587
I'm here to represent you.

